{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChFYiQMJbynLQBMn5onYG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[x] Running the stamp script after changing the `package.json` version updates both `plugin.yaml` and `SKILL.md`\n\nAll three checklist items are done and committed. `npm test` passes: 9 Node tests plus the Python suite.\n\n1. **Installed `plugin.yaml` and manifest versions:** the new test was red at first because `package.json` said `0.0.0` and `plugin.yaml` said `2.1.0`. I changed `package.json` to `2.1.0`, the version the plugin already had, so stamping doesn't drop the plugin back to `0.0.0`. The install manifest was already recording the package version. I also added the original attribution to `package.json` as `contributors`. Each name is written as `{name}` so npm doesn't read \"(garciacionet-alt)\" as a URL. `package-lock.json` still had the old worktree's name and no version, so I refreshed it with `npm i --package-lock-only`; only the top-level details changed.\n2. **Installed `SKILL.md` version:** this test passed as soon as I wrote it, because item 1 had already made the versions match. I checked that it fails if `SKILL.md`'s version is changed to something else.\n3. **Stamp script:** `scripts/stamp-version.ts` finds `package.json` and `tiiny-router/` relative to its own file. It rewrites the top-level `version:` line in `plugin.yaml` and the `version:` line in `SKILL.md`'s front matter, and stops with an error if either is missing. The `version` script in `package.json` runs it and stages both files, so `npm version <x>` commits them along with `package.json`. The test copies the files into a temporary directory, sets a new version, runs the script from another directory, and checks both files. It also checks that nothing else in `SKILL.md` changed. Running the script on the repo itself changes nothing, since everything is already at `2.1.0`.\n\nThe stamp script is TypeScript that `node` runs directly, so like the tests it needs Node >= 22.18 on a development machine. It isn't included in the published package.\n\n`docs/IMPLEMENTATION.md:55` has an example `plugin.yaml` showing `version: 2.1.0`. The script doesn't update it, so it will go stale after the next version bump; I left it as is. I added a short note on how versioning works to `AGENTS.md`, and my notes for this attempt are in `.redeye/notes.md`, uncommitted as instructed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1065,"cache_read_input_tokens":64865,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1065},"output_tokens":703,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"eea78a92-93ad-4b9c-b791-c68564bad39e","uuid":"94296584-26ef-44be-a24f-03e8a05d8b2c","timestamp":"2026-11-21T05:48:40.207Z","request_id":"req_011ChFYiQCNk8hNv7xVnDUCS"}
